<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ayah_circle - the end-of-ayah ornament (the ۝ rosette) that closes every verse.

  Drawn as a sixteen-petal rosette with an inner ring, exactly like the shape the Quran reader
  paints inside the page (AyahBadgeSpan builds the same geometry in code so it scales with the
  reader's text size). Nothing here is filled: the paper shows through, so the ayah number can sit
  on top of it and stay legible in either palette. That is also why the ornament is a separate
  layer from the number - see view_ayah_number_badge.xml, which stacks the two with identical
  bounds so the digits are centred by construction instead of by an offset that has to be tuned
  per screen density.
-->
